  n=7: brute=74/147 fit=74/147  match=True
  n=8: brute=63/128 fit=63/128  match=True
ALL MATCH (6/6, only 3 free params): True

======================================================================
STEP 3: recombine to get phi_n^{(2)} and check against THEOREM.md SS7.4 table
======================================================================
phi_n^{(2)} CLOSED FORM = (16*n**3 + n**2 + 21*n + 6)/(30*n**3)
apart (n -> infinity expansion): 8/15 + 1/(30*n) + 7/(10*n**2) + 1/(5*n**3)

phi_n^{(2)} - phi_2 = (n**2 + 21*n + 6)/(30*n**3)
apart: 1/(30*n) + 7/(10*n**2) + 1/(5*n**3)
=> leading order is Theta(1/n) [coefficient 1/30], NOT Theta(1/n^2).

verification against THEOREM.md SS7.4's own table (all 7 values, n=2..8):
  n=2: THEOREM.md=3/4 closed_form=3/4  match=True
  n=3: THEOREM.md=17/27 closed_form=17/27  match=True
  n=4: THEOREM.md=113/192 closed_form=113/192  match=True
  n=5: THEOREM.md=356/625 closed_form=356/625  match=True
  n=6: THEOREM.md=151/270 closed_form=151/270  match=True
  n=7: THEOREM.md=569/1029 closed_form=569/1029  match=True
  n=8: THEOREM.md=281/512 closed_form=281/512  match=True
ALL MATCH (including n=2, outside the n>K=2 derivation range): True
